  "instance_name": "Racial_Scapegoating",
  "label": "Racial Scapegoating",
  "description": "The practice of blaming a racial or ethnic group for societal problems or events, often to deflect responsibility or to incite division. In this meme, the false claim that 'African American leaders' organized the riots is an example of racial scapegoating, which attempts to shift blame onto Black communities for the chaos of the riots, ignoring the root causes of systemic racism and police brutality.",
